From faf9281542c4a87fc8b0f9a4b1a56178a794d4f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:31:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add r9fs suite: Rust r9fs vs C v9fs over the same QEMU
 virtio-9p export

qemu.bash exports R9FS_SHARE on two more virtio-9p devices: r9share,
and r9slow with throttled reads. The guest suite moves both from
9pnet_virtio to r9fs_virtio. It diffs an r9fs manifest (stat fields,
sha256, symlink targets) against the C v9fs view of the same host
directory through hostshare, then checks read-only/negative cases and
parallel reads. On r9slow it checks the kill latency of a reader
blocked on a posted request, and that unbinding the device fails that
request instead of delivering its reply.

v9fs-kmod loads the module (the chroot has no kmod).
v9fs-build-r9fs-kernel builds the Rust-enabled Image + r9fs.ko on the
host, since ghcr.io/v9fs/docker has no Rust toolchain. Not wired into
Actions yet.
